  "Bug_Title": "SING: Instance-getter method of class using singleton design pattern is not synchronized. (SING_SINGLETON_GETTER_NOT_SYNCHRONIZED)\uf0c1",
  "Bug_Details": "\nInstance-getter method of class using singleton design pattern is not synchronized. When this method is invoked by two or more threads simultaneously,\nmultiple instantiation of a singleton class becomes possible.\nSEI CERT MSC07-J rule\n",
  "Bug_Explanation": "The getInstance() method of Singleton class is not synchronized. This means that if two threads call getInstance() simultaneously, two instances of Singleton class can be created. This is a violation of the singleton design pattern.",
