    8
  ],
  "Seed_Compilation_Status": "Successful",
  "Trigger_Explanation": "The Singleton class uses the Singleton design pattern, which is a creation design pattern, that restricts the instantiation of a class to a single instance. The getInstance() method is made synchronized, ensuring that only one thread can execute the code inside the method at any given time. If this method is not synchronized, multiple threads can access it simultaneously, leading to multiple instances of the Singleton class.",
